<article class="env-lemma" id="0BI8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BI8">Lemma <span data-tag="0BI8">54.15.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a Noetherian scheme. Let $Y_ i \subset X$, $i = 1, \ldots , n$ be an integral closed subschemes of dimension $1$ each satisfying the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0BI4" data-tag="0BI4">54.15.1</a>. Then there exists a finite sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  X_ n \to X_{n - 1} \to \ldots \to X_1 \to X  \]
</div>
  <p> of blowups in closed points such that the strict transform $Y'_ i \subset X_ n$ of $Y_ i$ in $X_ n$ are pairwise disjoint regular curves. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0BI5" data-tag="0BI5">54.15.2</a> that we may assume $Y_ i$ is a regular curve for $i = 1, \ldots , n$. For every $i \not= j$ and $p \in Y_ i \cap Y_ j$ we have the invariant $m_ p(Y_ i \cap Y_ j)$ (<a href="/tag/0BI6" data-tag="0BI6">54.15.2.1</a>). If the maximum of these numbers is $> 1$, then we can decrease it (Lemma <a href="/tag/0BI7" data-tag="0BI7">54.15.3</a>) by blowing up in all the points $p$ where the maximum is attained. If the maximum is $1$ then we can separate the curves using the same lemma by blowing up in all these points $p$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>